        "geology": "Miocene molassic deposits: calcareous, clayey and sandy\r\n\r\n",
        "hydrology": "The hydrological regime is pluvial with low water period from june to november. Important flash floods occur in december-january, but the most significant one are observed in May or June. The impermeable substratum favorise rapid water, nutirents and contaminants during flood events. The groundwaters are limited, mainly located in the alluvial deposits and in some sand lends in the middle slope. The evapotranspiration is very high and the runoff coefficient is very low (15% on average). Consequently, during the driest years, intermittent flows may occur during the summer period.",
        "soils": "Calcareous and silty-clayeye soils",
        "vegetation": "Cultures: wheat, sunflower, rapeseed in rotation with introduction of a cover crop before a summer crop"
      },
